-- title:
--   Type preservation on the Bruhat–Tits tree and parity of v(det)
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring, and let $K_0$ be a field equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R_0$; let $\varpi_0 \in R_0$ be irreducible. Consider the vertex set [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex R₀ K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) of homothety classes of full $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2$, with the graph `BruhatTits.tree R₀ K₀` whose adjacency is generated by the relation ‘the classes have representatives $L$, $L'$ with $L$, $L'$ adjacent lattices’, and the base vertex [`LT.LatticeTree.stdVertex R₀ K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L358), the class of the lattice of vectors both of whose coordinates are integral over $R_0$. Let $G$ be a group with a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ and an action of $G$ on the vertex set satisfying $g \cdot x = \rho(g)\cdot x$ for all $g$ and $x$. Let $g \in G$, let $m \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with $\rho(g)$ equal to the projective class of $m$, and suppose $\det m = u\,\varpi_0^{\,k}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u \in R_0^{\times}$ and some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ (images taken under the structure map $R_0 \to K_0$). Then $g$ belongs to the subgroup of elements $h$ with $\mathrm{dist}(v_0, h\cdot w) \equiv \mathrm{dist}(v_0,w) \pmod 2$ for every vertex $w$, where $v_0$ is the standard vertex, if and only if $k$ is even.
--
--   This is Serre's description of the two types (colours) of vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a discretely valued field, together with the identification of the type-preserving subgroup — the elements acting without inversion — as the kernel of $g \mapsto v(\det g) \bmod 2$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd and Mumford-uniformisation part of the development, for instance in the passage to the even part of a lattice of matrices and in statements about invariant fields for the action on the $p$-adic upper half plane.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_BruhatTits_mem_typePreserving_iff_even_of_det_eq_mul_zpow.lean

